{
  "circuit_type": "H-bridge",
  "summary": "This is a full H-bridge circuit using four thyristors (Th1, Th2, Th3, Th4) and four antiparallel diodes (D1, D2, D3, D4) to control the direction and magnitude of current through a load. The input voltage V is applied across the top and bottom rails. The load is connected between the two midpoint nodes of the H-bridge. Current flows through the load in one direction when Th1 and Th4 are conducting, and in the opposite direction when Th2 and Th3 are conducting. The diodes provide a freewheeling path for inductive loads.",
