  "topology": "The H-bridge consists of two legs. The top leg has Th1 and Th3, with D1 and D3 as antiparallel diodes. The bottom leg has Th2 and Th4, with D2 and D4 as antiparallel diodes. The load is connected between the midpoints of the two legs (N3 and N4). The input voltage V is applied across the top and bottom rails. The diodes provide a freewheeling path for inductive loads.",
